                        "form": "kedged"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ff948fde-bdb8-34cd-a4eb-dc10bcea35a3",
                        "entry_id": "73f03261-9c06-3264-a0b9-6c4a1d178ca7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To warp (a vessel) by carrying out a kedge in a boat, dropping it overboard, and hauling the vessel up to it."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "efe97172-3268-3ee4-83b6-a47ac816019e",
                        "entry_id": "73f03261-9c06-3264-a0b9-6c4a1d178ca7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To move with the help of a kedge, as described above."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "intransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d747c24f-940c-4bab-802e-c35d01643ad5",
                                "sense_id": "efe97172-3268-3ee4-83b6-a47ac816019e",
                                "text": "[…] there was a stretch of twelve miles of channel running in a north-easterly direction which the ship could not possibly negotiate under sail unless a change of wind should occur — of which there seemed to be absolutely no prospect. The only alternative, therefore, would be to kedge those twelve miles; truly a most formidable undertaking for four persons — one of them being a girl — to attempt."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9840ecaa-18cb-49d9-9bee-986b6d1d2e42",
                                "sense_id": "efe97172-3268-3ee4-83b6-a47ac816019e",
                                "text": "By noon the men had loaded the cargo & Prophetess was kedging out of the bay against unfavourable winds."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5ff1775b-49e8-4251-80fc-b3c9ae1d6bae",
                        "source_entry_id": "73f03261-9c06-3264-a0b9-6c4a1d178ca7",
                        "source_sense_description": "transitive",
                        "target_lang_word": "touer",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "touer",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a955a1e1-d83a-382a-83b5-9945e6dfeb50",
                                        "entry_id": "a944f348-8753-35b7-9cfa-fb252c1de710",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Faire avancer un navire en le tirant, haler une péniche, remorquer un navire, paumoyer une barque, etc."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2a968a0a-aec0-4eda-ba5a-6ecf20d502d4",
                                                "sense_id": "a955a1e1-d83a-382a-83b5-9945e6dfeb50",
                                                "text": "Aussitôt un officier est envoyé auprès du gouverneur (...). Sa mission est de remercier en mon nom, M. le gouverneur de son attention délicate de nous envoyer ses chaloupes pour nous touer dans le port."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f4647b14-225d-45aa-af0c-e92ebdc2d852",
                                                "sense_id": "a955a1e1-d83a-382a-83b5-9945e6dfeb50",
                                                "text": "En route, il arriva une péripétie. Nous touions, du verbe touer (rien à voir avec les touillettes), quand, sorti d'on ne sait où, un citoyen vint se mettre en travers du chemin."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1cf5e3cc-3c3d-3c27-9174-bf78fbda7e40",
                                        "entry_id": "a944f348-8753-35b7-9cfa-fb252c1de710",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Se remorquer."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "196eaf39-d036-4eb4-bf0f-9fb29167f2db",
                                                "sense_id": "1cf5e3cc-3c3d-3c27-9174-bf78fbda7e40",
                                                "text": "Se touer pour sortir d’un port, d’une rivière."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "40255a46-d262-4904-8487-8e1b60723093",
                                                "sense_id": "1cf5e3cc-3c3d-3c27-9174-bf78fbda7e40",
                                                "text": "Si malheureusement un vaisseau se trouvait engagé dans les Abrolhos, il ne devrait pas pour cela se croire perdu. Il faudrait y mouiller. On trouve communément au pied des récifs cinq à six brasses d’eau, fond de vase blanchâtre. On en sortirait en se touant."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
